    "['interface [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interfaces ge-1/0/0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interfaces ge-1/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent for the specified Huawei command:\\n\\n##\\ninterfaces ge-1/0/0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper uses \"interfaces\" (plural) instead of \"interface\"\\n- \"GigabitEthernet\" is shortened to \"ge\" in Juniper\\n- The interface numbering format remains the same (1/0/0) though Juniper typically uses a slightly different syntax (1/0/0 instead of 1/0/0.0 for logical units)\\n- Juniper doesn\\'t require the \"undo shutdown\" equivalent at this stage as interfaces are enabled by default', 'trans_template': 'interfaces ge-1/0/0'}]]": 1,
    "['undo [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete interfaces GigabitEthernet 1/0/0 disable', 'parent_command': ['interfaces ge-1/0/0'], 'root': 'interfaces ge-1/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ndelete interfaces GigabitEthernet 1/0/0 disable\\ndelete interfaces GigabitEthernet 2/0/0 disable\\n##\\n\\nExplanation: \\n- The HUAWEI `undo shutdown` command enables an interface that was previously administratively shut down. \\n- The Juniper equivalent is `delete disable` on the interface, which removes any administrative shutdown configuration.\\n- I included both interface translations since the original configuration had `undo shutdown` on two interfaces (GigabitEthernet 1/0/0 and 2/0/0).', 'trans_template': 'delete interfaces GigabitEthernet 1/0/0 disable'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete interfaces GigabitEthernet 2/0/0 disable', 'parent_command': ['interfaces ge-1/0/0'], 'root': 'interfaces ge-1/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ndelete interfaces GigabitEthernet 1/0/0 disable\\ndelete interfaces GigabitEthernet 2/0/0 disable\\n##\\n\\nExplanation: \\n- The HUAWEI `undo shutdown` command enables an interface that was previously administratively shut down. \\n- The Juniper equivalent is `delete disable` on the interface, which removes any administrative shutdown configuration.\\n- I included both interface translations since the original configuration had `undo shutdown` on two interfaces (GigabitEthernet 1/0/0 and 2/0/0).', 'trans_template': 'delete interfaces GigabitEthernet 2/0/0 disable'}]]": 1,
