    "['binding tunnel [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 172.20.1.1/24', 'parent_command': ['interfaces ge-1/0/0'], 'root': 'interfaces ge-1/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `binding tunnel gre` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 172.20.1.1/24\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source 172.20.1.1\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination 172.21.1.2\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel protocol gre\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, GRE tunnel configuration is typically done directly on the physical interface (or logical unit) rather than having a separate \"binding\" command. The equivalent configuration requires setting up the tunnel parameters directly on the interface.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 172.20.1.1/24'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source 172.20.1.1', 'parent_command': ['interfaces ge-1/0/0'], 'root': 'interfaces ge-1/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `binding tunnel gre` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 172.20.1.1/24\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source 172.20.1.1\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination 172.21.1.2\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel protocol gre\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, GRE tunnel configuration is typically done directly on the physical interface (or logical unit) rather than having a separate \"binding\" command. The equivalent configuration requires setting up the tunnel parameters directly on the interface.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source 172.20.1.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination 172.21.1.2', 'parent_command': ['interfaces ge-1/0/0'], 'root': 'interfaces ge-1/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `binding tunnel gre` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 172.20.1.1/24\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source 172.20.1.1\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination 172.21.1.2\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel protocol gre\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, GRE tunnel configuration is typically done directly on the physical interface (or logical unit) rather than having a separate \"binding\" command. The equivalent configuration requires setting up the tunnel parameters directly on the interface.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination 172.21.1.2'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel protocol gre', 'parent_command': ['interfaces ge-1/0/0'], 'root': 'interfaces ge-1/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `binding tunnel gre` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet address 172.20.1.1/24\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel source 172.20.1.1\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel destination 172.21.1.2\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel protocol gre\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, GRE tunnel configuration is typically done directly on the physical interface (or logical unit) rather than having a separate \"binding\" command. The equivalent configuration requires setting up the tunnel parameters directly on the interface.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet tunnel protocol gre'}]]": 1,
